            "location": "src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts",
            "message": "gitEnvironment is reached only via fixtures.ts#fixture/git (a test helper), and fixtures.ts is not itself listed as a file in the build gate's test record, so this path is present-but-unverified rather than confirmed passing — it is likely exercised indirectly by the passing adversarial.test.ts/source.test.ts/subject.test.ts suites that consume these fixtures, but the gate cannot confirm that directly.",
            "expectationRef": "gitEnvironment",
            "confidence": "observation",
            "findingKind": "symbol-coverage",
            "symbolId": "335061"
          },
          {
            "dimension": "coverage",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/workflow/code-review/investigation/work.ts",
            "message": "readApprovedWork is reached only via fixtures.ts#subjectFixture (a test helper), and fixtures.ts is not itself listed as a file in the build gate's test record, so this path is present-but-unverified rather than confirmed passing — it is likely exercised indirectly by the passing subject.test.ts/source.test.ts suites that consume this fixture, but the gate cannot confirm that directly.",
            "expectationRef": "readApprovedWork",
            "confidence": "observation",
            "findingKind": "symbol-coverage",
            "symbolId": "335136"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "dimension": "quality",
        "findings": [
          {
            "dimension": "quality",
            "severity": "MED",
            "location": "src/workflow/code-review/investigation/git-packets.ts:199",
            "message": "readCommitPacket (and its helpers assertOid, decodeUtf8, assertRepoPath, rawChanges, span, add, plus ReviewGitReader.command/object/commit) show no reaching tests in the graph, and readCommitPacket itself has no recorded callers. git-packets.test.ts only calls the `fixture` helper — none of the new diff-parsing or commit-digest logic appears to be exercised by an assertion. This may be a grounding gap on a newly-added file rather than a true coverage hole, but it's worth confirming the test file actually invokes readCommitPacket/ReviewGitReader before trusting this module's parsing of untrusted git pack bytes (span offsets, rawChanges tab-splitting, decodeObject header checks).",
            "counterpartRef": "",
            "confidence": "observation"
          },
          {
            "dimension": "quality",
            "severity": "MED",
            "location": "src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts:62",
            "message": "createGitRunner's abort()/stop()/settle() trio has no reaching tests (onAbort, abort, settle, stop all show empty testsReaching), and readPinnedSources itself has no recorded callers. abort() calls stop() which calls settle(error) to reject the in-flight promise, but settle() is presumably also invoked on normal process exit inside readPinnedSources; if an AbortSignal fires concurrently with process completion there is no visible guard preventing settle from being invoked twice or a completed read being silently discarded. Given this handles cancellation of a native git subprocess, that race path should be covered by a test, not left to the empty-grounding default.",
            "counterpartRef": "",
            "confidence": "observation"
          },
          {
            "dimension": "quality",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/design/corpus/sources/git-reader.ts:120",
            "message": "abortRead() has no recorded callers and no callees — it reads as a leftover/unused exported helper rather than wired-in functionality. If it isn't referenced by anything outside this graph slice, it should be removed rather than kept as dead code.",
            "counterpartRef": "",
            "confidence": "observation"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
